question_stem:
A mass is suspended vertically from a fixed point by means of a spring, as illustrated in Fig. 4.1.

{{figure:9702_w19_41_q04_figure_4_1}}

The mass is oscillating vertically. The variation with displacement $x$ of the acceleration $a$ of the mass is shown in Fig. 4.2.

{{figure:9702_w19_41_q04_figure_4_2}}

parts.text:
The maximum speed of the mass when oscillating with simple harmonic motion of amplitude $x_0$ is $v_0$.

On Fig. 4.3, show the variation with displacement $x$ of the velocity $v$ of the mass for displacements from $+x_0$ to $-x_0$.

{{figure:9702_w19_41_q04_figure_4_3}}
